{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1492254-v20-domain-background","id":1492254,"title":"V20 Domain Background","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-09-03T14:18:54-07:00","id":1492254,"title":"V20 Domain Background","content":"I'm wondering a bit about the rules for the Domain background. Specifically about the reduced difficulty for your hunting checks.<br /> <br /> Is that reduction dependent on the points that you put in the size of your domain or on the overall point in your of the domain background (size+security).<br /> <br /> To me it sounds reads like the latter was the case, and like the size has no mechanical benefit.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5199-aahz","name":"Aahz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-04T04:45:56-07:00","id":1492289,"title":"","content":"Domain is a Background that is trying to simulate too many things at once and doesn't have enough mechanical room to do any of them well. Furthermore, since Backgrounds don't function like normal abilities or attributes that means they can be gained, expanded, and lost as the story progresses without XP being a factor.<br /> <br /> The size of one's Domain has no direct mechanical benefit, only narrative benefits which have the possibility to lead to mechanical benefits later on. By this I mean the area you control can have other benefits.<br /> <br /> For instance, let's say that your Kindred wanted to be in control of the Docks in their city. Well depending on the size of the docks and how important a trade hub the city is, you would need Domain *** to Domain **** to represent this due to size.<br /> <br /> But being in control of the docks means you can demand kickbacks from the dock workers unions, any organized crime groups that want to move contraband through there, and of course bribes from more legitimate business who want their goods given priority for clearing customs or being shipped out. Thus, this leads to the Docks which is a Domain generating Resources.<br /> <br /> Since the World of Darkness is a darker and grittier version of our own world, then in all likelihood there will be some human trafficking going on, which means you potentially can have essentially a shipping container or three full of people with no rights or records. This can function as a hunting ground or potentially a Herd background if you have something like Dominate or Presence. Without the human trafficking however, unless you are drinking fish blood or feeding on the guards, pickings will be scarce.<br /> <br /> As far as security goes, that once again is more of a narrative aspect than a mechanical one. The Docks could just be a small series of open-air piers with a couple warehouses nearby that is watched over by a harbor master. The Docks could alternatively be a huge area with loads of fences, security cameras, guards, and customs officials, making it remarkably secure. All of this then scales the benefits in other areas.<br /> <br /> By controlling such a key area, this means you are the person to go to for favors regarding transport, thus potentially earning you Fame, Status, and Influence background points.<br /> <br /> Properly played, Backgrounds tend to grow like weeds and give access to other Backgrounds quite quickly. But at the same time if the ST or the Players don't bother to extrapolate the potential benefits and story hooks from having such a location, then it doesn't really matter much.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-04T15:26:51-07:00","id":1492321,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1492254-v20-domain-background?p=1492289#post1492289\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Domain is a Background that is trying to simulate too many things at once and doesn't have enough mechanical room to do any of them well. Furthermore, since Backgrounds don't function like normal abilities or attributes that means they can be gained, expanded, and lost as the story progresses without XP being a factor.<br /> <br /> The size of one's Domain has no direct mechanical benefit, only narrative benefits which have the possibility to lead to mechanical benefits later on. By this I mean the area you control can have other benefits.<br /> <br /> For instance, let's say that your Kindred wanted to be in control of the Docks in their city. Well depending on the size of the docks and how important a trade hub the city is, you would need Domain *** to Domain **** to represent this due to size.<br /> <br /> But being in control of the docks means you can demand kickbacks from the dock workers unions, any organized crime groups that want to move contraband through there, and of course bribes from more legitimate business who want their goods given priority for clearing customs or being shipped out. Thus, this leads to the Docks which is a Domain generating Resources.<br /> <br /> Since the World of Darkness is a darker and grittier version of our own world, then in all likelihood there will be some human trafficking going on, which means you potentially can have essentially a shipping container or three full of people with no rights or records. This can function as a hunting ground or potentially a Herd background if you have something like Dominate or Presence. Without the human trafficking however, unless you are drinking fish blood or feeding on the guards, pickings will be scarce.<br /> <br /> As far as security goes, that once again is more of a narrative aspect than a mechanical one. The Docks could just be a small series of open-air piers with a couple warehouses nearby that is watched over by a harbor master. The Docks could alternatively be a huge area with loads of fences, security cameras, guards, and customs officials, making it remarkably secure. All of this then scales the benefits in other areas.<br /> <br /> By controlling such a key area, this means you are the person to go to for favors regarding transport, thus potentially earning you Fame, Status, and Influence background points.<br /> <br /> Properly played, Backgrounds tend to grow like weeds and give access to other Backgrounds quite quickly. But at the same time if the ST or the Players don't bother to extrapolate the potential benefits and story hooks from having such a location, then it doesn't really matter much.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure about other editions, but V20 specifies that the only thing domain gives you control over is feeding rights among your fellow parasites. You don't have any control over the area so far as mortal society is concerned.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Kindred who claims the domain can\u2019t keep the<br /> living inhabitants from going about their business,<br /> nor does she exercise any direct influence over them,<br /> but she can keep watch herself and mind their comings<br /> and goings. She can also have Allies or Retainers<br /> specifically look for unfamiliar vampires and alert her<br /> when they find some. </div> </div> </div><br /> The kind of things you are talking about would seem to fall under something like 'influence: The docks'.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-04T21:29:18-07:00","id":1492339,"title":"","content":"The main appeal for domain is security. Having the docks doesn't mean you've become capable of runing an empire there, you were capable before that. However, if you set your haven up by the docs, organized some intricate system with the locals, and THEN the domain is legaly given to someone else... that's a rough time.<br /> <br /> Also if you're just &quot;there&quot; it's free competition, if it's actually yours then anyone who wants to be there is going to be owing you a favour. Most princes will honour your right to punish whoever intrudes in your domain to an extent. <br /> You can have a stake in enterprises or control mortals out of the domain. That's not a problem. But the essentials to your living should ideally be within your Domain. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-05T00:22:47-07:00","id":1492348,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mizu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1492254-v20-domain-background?p=1492321#post1492321\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not sure about other editions, but V20 specifies that the only thing domain gives you control over is feeding rights among your fellow parasites. You don't have any control over the area so far as mortal society is concerned</div> </div> </div> </div>Domain was an attempt in V20 to condense down other older edition Backgrounds into one and it didn't quite stick the landing. The feeding rights is kind of a Herd thing, while the security aspect is from the optional Haven background. But in the description of Domain it mentions specific things like having control over a high-rise apartment building, but that is more a question of Resources to buy ownership or just a matter of ghouling the owner or using Dominate to transfer ownership.<br /> <br /> The security aspects in particular is kind of non-functional because it doesn't exactly say how the security works. Anyone with a high Resources score can simply hire security guards, but how do you have security and maintain feeding exclusivity if you are neither rich, nor powerful? This is a key distinction because your security affects both supernatural and mortal visitors.<br /> <br /> Technically Domain can model a haven, a personal public hunting ground, and to a certain extent territory claimed such as pooled Domain meaning an entire city is claimed. But the costs and variety of scenarios means it is a poor emulation tool. For instance if you own a home that is your haven with people living there to munch on, do you simulate that by taking one dot in Domain or do you get that by taking one dot in Herd and a few dots in Resources?<br /> <br /> If you own a hospital, is that a Domain for feeding at the blood bank, an explanation for having Resources five, a necromantic ritual parts shop, or just backstory fluff regarding why you were selected for the embrace? Depending how you answer, that then means that certain choices or avenues get locked off in your game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-05T00:36:22-07:00","id":1492349,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1492254-v20-domain-background?p=1492339#post1492339\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The main appeal for domain is security. Having the docks doesn't mean you've become capable of runing an empire there, you were capable before that. However, if you set your haven up by the docs, organized some intricate system with the locals, and THEN the domain is legaly given to someone else... that's a rough time.<br /> <br /> Also if you're just &quot;there&quot; it's free competition, if it's actually yours then anyone who wants to be there is going to be owing you a favour. Most princes will honour your right to punish whoever intrudes in your domain to an extent.<br /> You can have a stake in enterprises or control mortals out of the domain. That's not a problem. But the essentials to your living should ideally be within your Domain.</div> </div> </div> </div>Random question, using your take on Domain, how would you model a Kindred businessman? I bring this up because the fluff routinely brings up how rich Kindred can be, and how they will select mortals who are accomplished in these areas for the embrace, thus a neonate having a high Resources score and owning many properties/businesses shouldn't be particularly rare.<br /> <br /> But when you try to model it using the system, you pick up Resources 5 and then burn out all your freebie points trying to map out all the places you own because they won't always be in one easy to define location. I bring this up because IRL when buying property, you invest wherever is available rather than exclusively buying in just one neighborhood. This only gets compounded when you own property in different cities, states, or countries.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-05T00:47:29-07:00","id":1492350,"title":"","content":"It is kind of wonky, but it does answer that question by suggesting that a high security area could simply be a place with limited access routes that are easier for your character to keep tabs on. Like maybe for example a 2 dot domain is a large apartment building whose superintendent doesn't bother having a security guy in the lobby while a 3 (2 size+1 security) dot is an apartment building who has a security guy in the lobby that will raise an attention drawing fuss (despite not being in your employ) your character will notice if some stranger waltzes in being all creepy. Or one example in the book of a 4 dot was a community that can only be accessed by a single bridge you can watch. So I agree it is kind of clunky but not completely impossible as described.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":988,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","user":"Mizu","date":". 09-05-2022, 03:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-05T01:33:08-07:00","id":1492351,"title":"","content":"IDK about that. Domain as in -your territory is recognized by the relevant authorities- is a fair concept and a worthy background to buy. If you could just buy anything with money and claim it as yours then the city is going to be 100 times less stable. Imagine you ghouled the owner of a company and set up your haven in his building, then one day he dies and the inheritor has been ghouled by someone else. Moving through mortal legal documents to decide who owns what is politically a pain in the ass, just declaring who owns what swath of land however, is simple, effective, and keeps the amount of bullshit down.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-05T01:36:03-07:00","id":1492352,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1492254-v20-domain-background?p=1492349#post1492349\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Random question, using your take on Domain, how would you model a Kindred businessman? I bring this up because the fluff routinely brings up how rich Kindred can be, and how they will select mortals who are accomplished in these areas for the embrace, thus a neonate having a high Resources score and owning many properties/businesses shouldn't be particularly rare.<br /> <br /> But when you try to model it using the system, you pick up Resources 5 and then burn out all your freebie points trying to map out all the places you own because they won't always be in one easy to define location. I bring this up because IRL when buying property, you invest wherever is available rather than exclusively buying in just one neighborhood. This only gets compounded when you own property in different cities, states, or countries.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well I said this didn't I? <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">You can have a stake in enterprises or control mortals out of the domain. That's not a problem. But the essentials to your living should ideally be within your Domain.</span></span></span> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-05T08:00:51-07:00","id":1492366,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1492254-v20-domain-background?p=1492351#post1492351\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">IDK about that. Domain as in -your territory is recognized by the relevant authorities- is a fair concept and a worthy background to buy. If you could just buy anything with money and claim it as yours then the city is going to be 100 times less stable. Imagine you ghouled the owner of a company and set up your haven in his building, then one day he dies and the inheritor has been ghouled by someone else. Moving through mortal legal documents to decide who owns what is politically a pain in the ass, just declaring who owns what swath of land however, is simple, effective, and keeps the amount of bullshit down.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, no, and maybe.<br /> <br /> Any vampire can ghoul a business owner, which can mean you have to keep an eye on succession rights, except that vampires are expected to move around to avoid the &quot;not aging thing&quot; being noticed, so theoretically any business minded vampire would have that taken care of within a couple weeks of taking over the company rather than leaving it an open-ended issue for some other kindred to exploit.<br /> <br /> All it takes is to sign the business over to a holding company you own, as per the rights of the original owner to make that choice, which cuts any inheritors out of the picture. When you apply IRL best business practices to the storyline, it really is no more BS than expecting combat players to keep track of ammo in their guns during a fight.<br /> <br /> The ability to buy businesses or just buy land and build new businesses doesn't cause instability in a city, mostly because most cities already have established kindred who have done this long ago, so only individual companies or plots of land will come up for sale at any given time. Sure, most elders could buy all the burger joints in town, but that isn't valuable enough to be worth their time, but it would be valuable to a neonate trying to establish a power base. Alternatively, those same elders could just as easily be looking to offload an underperforming property or business.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-05T08:27:53-07:00","id":1492368,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mizu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1492254-v20-domain-background?p=1492350#post1492350\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It is kind of wonky, but it does answer that question by suggesting that a high security area could simply be a place with limited access routes that are easier for your character to keep tabs on. Like maybe for example a 2 dot domain is a large apartment building whose superintendent doesn't bother having a security guy in the lobby while a 3 (2 size+1 security) dot is an apartment building who has a security guy in the lobby that will raise an attention drawing fuss (despite not being in your employ) your character will notice if some stranger waltzes in being all creepy. Or one example in the book of a 4 dot was a community that can only be accessed by a single bridge you can watch. So I agree it is kind of clunky but not completely impossible as described.</div> </div> </div> </div>An example from a different thread on the subject of Resources is a decommissioned missile silo. There are dozens of these things scattered across the US and are being sold off to civilians. The going price is about $350,000 which gets you the entire structure and the surrounding land. With Resources 5 rating, a one-million-dollar purchase is not going to drop your Resource rating. The whole silo can be converted to luxury apocalypse bunker for another say $500,000 which means you still have another $150,000 left over to invest in goodies or supernatural grade defenses.<br /> <br /> Now this Silo, the prices and capacities of which are based of IRL luxury bunker conversions, can support you, your coterie, a permanent live in Herd, and a private security force on site for up to five years without additional supplies. Technically speaking it should count as your Haven but given the fact you can feed there, and it has impressive security functions, it could count as a Domain 3 just for being the size of a high rise except underground, but the enhanced security features would bump that up to a full Domain 5.<br /> <br /> Yes, this is an extreme example of security that is outside the average city, but in truth it is technically cheaper than your average celebrity buying a multi-million-dollar mansion, which no one would debate your average Ventrue, Toreador, or Giovanni owning several such houses across the world, probably inside gated communities.<br /> <br /> Claimed Territory (street gang holding certain street corners) is different than Owned Territory (you own the factory), just as your Haven is not the same as businesses that you own, though any of them could function as a backup haven.<br /> <br /> VtM really wants you to play the Lost Boys, rather than capable business owners, despite the majority of elders having vast economic empires at their command. It's almost like no one is expected to survive the game long enough to get to the point where that kind of power building is a consideration.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-05T09:57:16-07:00","id":1492372,"title":"","content":"I think you're underestimating what a horrendous system that is. Rivals would deliberately try to sweep up businesses by ghouling inheritors and forcing out the current owner, or by ghouling a guy and influencing shareholders to make him the new CEO. There are countless ways to do this cleverly. So even in the most wretched of Anarch states folk are going to lay claim to Turf and they're not going to bother about who actually controls the finances. Most Camarilla vampires crave stability, and constant squables make the prince look weak and ineffectual. Ergo something like &quot;The Hospital and these three blocks to the south of it are Erin's domain, she has the authority to dictate how other kindred, bar the I prince, use it. Anyone entering without her permision has commited a crime. It's hers till she lets or sells it or I the prince decide otherwise&quot; is essential to forming stable cities. That's a very extreme example but the point is Everyone's allowed to buy property in the area or send proxies in, but even if bob bought everything within Erin's Domain, it's still her domain. Bob doesn't get the right to set up a haven or feed in Erin's domain just because he or his proxies own everything within. <br /> <br /> Domain is a tradition with wildly different interpretations from city to city. But the point of the background is that people recognize a vampire's territory and know that if they act up within that territory it's only right that the Domain holder can act in retribution. By acknowledging X's domain, they can expect X to acknowledge Y's domain, and so on and so forth. This is a virtuous cycle and keeps vampires beyond arms length and therefore civil. If it were up to who owns what in the mortal world, the Ventrue get culled repeatedly, because nobody would be able to withstand that shit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-05T11:27:55-07:00","id":1492377,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1492254-v20-domain-background?p=1492372#post1492372\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think you're underestimating what a horrendous system that is. Rivals would deliberately try to sweep up businesses by ghouling inheritors and forcing out the current owner, or by ghouling a guy and influencing shareholders to make him the new CEO. There are countless ways to do this cleverly.\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>No, I understand how much upheaval that can cause in the beginning, that is good old fashioned economic warfare. The type that has been in fashion for literally millennia. The benefit of the modern age is that once you gain control over something like this you can set it up so bloodbonding some one new won't do your rivals any good. Just out of curiosity, have your read the VtM suplement &quot;Gilded Cage&quot; it was published back in 2001? It more or less covers all of this stuff.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1492254-v20-domain-background?p=1492372#post1492372\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So even in the most wretched of Anarch states folk are going to lay claim to Turf and they're not going to bother about who actually controls the finances. Most Camarilla vampires crave stability, and constant squables make the prince look weak and ineffectual. Ergo something like &quot;The Hospital and these three blocks to the south of it are Erin's domain, she has the authority to dictate how other kindred, bar the I prince, use it. Anyone entering without her permision has commited a crime. It's hers till she lets or sells it or I the prince decide otherwise&quot; is essential to forming stable cities. That's a very extreme example but the point is Everyone's allowed to buy property in the area or send proxies in, but even if bob bought everything within Erin's Domain, it's still her domain. Bob doesn't get the right to set up a haven or feed in Erin's domain just because he or his proxies own everything within.</div> </div> </div> </div>If the Camarilla vampires craved stability, they would not have Brujah or Malkavians as members, to say nothing of the Nosferatu leatherface contingent. Hell, if the Camarilla wanted peace and quiet, they would outlaw Harpies. As for the Prince, their job is to enforce the masquerade, not to play property court. Yes they can declare an area Elysium or off limits as hunting grounds, but they don't technically have the power to force you to sell your haven or business interests, thus if you own a business that happens to be in some one elses Domain, you visiting your business is between you and the other kindred, not the prince.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1492254-v20-domain-background?p=1492372#post1492372\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Domain is a tradition with wildly different interpretations from city to city. But the point of the background is that people recognize a vampire's territory and know that if they act up within that territory it's only right that the Domain holder can act in retribution. By acknowledging X's domain, they can expect X to acknowledge Y's domain, and so on and so forth. This is a virtuous cycle and keeps vampires beyond arms length and therefore civil. If it were up to who owns what in the mortal world, the Ventrue get culled repeatedly, because nobody would be able to withstand that shit.</div> </div> </div> </div>Domain the Background is not the same as Domain the Tradition. One is a mechanic while the other is a societal law that no one actually follows.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-05T11:58:17-07:00","id":1492378,"title":"","content":"Of course the camarilla is going to have the Brujah and Malks. You think it would be smarter to go against them?<br /> <br /> (Malkavians probably cause less problems than Toreador mind you, PC fishmalks excluded)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-05T13:05:30-07:00","id":1492384,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1492254-v20-domain-background?p=1492348#post1492348\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Technically Domain can model a haven, a personal public hunting ground, and to a certain extent territory claimed such as pooled Domain meaning an entire city is claimed. But the costs and variety of scenarios means it is a poor emulation tool. For instance if you own a home that is your haven with people living there to munch on, do you simulate that by taking one dot in Domain or do you get that by taking one dot in Herd and a few dots in Resources?<br /> <br /> If you own a hospital, is that a Domain for feeding at the blood bank, an explanation for having Resources five, a necromantic ritual parts shop, or just backstory fluff regarding why you were selected for the embrace? Depending how you answer, that then means that certain choices or avenues get locked off in your game.</div> </div> </div> </div>Domain means that you still have to activly hunt for the blood, the herd just gives you a certain amount of blood each day.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5199-aahz","name":"Aahz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-05T13:19:39-07:00","id":1492386,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1492254-v20-domain-background?p=1492368#post1492368\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now this Silo, the prices and capacities of which are based of IRL luxury bunker conversions, can support you, your coterie, a permanent live in Herd, and a private security force on site for up to five years without additional supplies. Technically speaking it should count as your Haven but given the fact you can feed there, and it has impressive security functions, it could count as a Domain 3 just for being the size of a high rise except underground, but the enhanced security features would bump that up to a full Domain 5.</div> </div> </div> </div>Since all humans that live there are either your herd, your retainers or maybe part of your military force back ground. That's is clearly a heaven not a domain.<br /> <br /> But there is some wired overlapp between Heaven, Ressources and Domain. And I think that comes partly from Heaven being added in later book and not being part of the core rules.<br /> <br /> If we just stick with the core Backgrounds, Buildings you leagally own are part of Ressources, while a Domain is a Territory that you claim, with that claim beeing usually recognized by the Kindred<br /> authority in that city, but you usually don't own.<br /> <br /> And honesly I think Heaven is something that should be part of your resource background.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5199-aahz","name":"Aahz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-05T17:56:47-07:00","id":1492404,"title":"","content":"I don't use Domain or Haven in my games. The haven is just part of the Resources background. The Domain is an in-game situation. Normally my players start without any Domain and can earn areas of control (simulated with Influence), which can be sanctioned, or not by the Prince, or exclusive hunting grounds that decrease the difficulty of hunting rills","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27429-microcuchon","name":"Microcuchon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"201"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}